[
  {
    "@comment": "An order with its customer and the participants of all its events, combined in KrakenD config. Calls run in order: 0 the order; 1 its customer ({resp0_customer_id}); 2 the order's events, whose participant_ids lists the backend-level flatmap gathers into one list; 3 those users in one batch call ({resp2_participant_ids}). Duplicates in the gathered list are harmless: /users?ids= returns each matching user once.",
    "endpoint": "/v1/orders/{id}",
    "method": "GET",
    "output_encoding": "json",
    "extra_config": {
      "proxy": {
        "sequential": true,
        "flatmap_filter": [
          {
            "type": "del",
            "args": [
              "participant_ids"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "del",
            "args": [
              "requested"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "del",
            "args": [
              "returned"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "del",
            "args": [
              "missing"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "backend": [
      {
        "url_pattern": "/orders/{id}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      },
      {
        "url_pattern": "/users/{resp0_customer_id}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "group": "customer",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      },
      {
        "@comment": "flatmap has no 'for each': gathering takes one operation per event, so this handles up to 5 events per order and ignores the rest. Slots with no event are skipped. Wildcards address all events but cannot collect from them: move from events.*.participant_ids keeps only the last list, and append ignores wildcards.",
        "url_pattern": "/events?order_id={id}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ],
        "extra_config": {
          "proxy": {
            "flatmap_filter": [
              {
                "type": "move",
                "args": [
                  "events.0.participant_ids",
                  "participant_ids"
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "append",
                "args": [
                  "events.1.participant_ids",
                  "participant_ids"
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "append",
                "args": [
                  "events.2.participant_ids",
                  "participant_ids"
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "append",
                "args": [
                  "events.3.participant_ids",
                  "participant_ids"
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "append",
                "args": [
                  "events.4.participant_ids",
                  "participant_ids"
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "del",
                "args": [
                  "events.*.order_id"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@comment": "For an order with no events there is no participant_ids to substitute, so the placeholder goes upstream unresolved. It matches no user, so participants is empty \u2014 correct \u2014 but it would be listed in `missing`, which is why the endpoint drops `missing`.",
        "url_pattern": "/users?ids={resp2_participant_ids}",
        "encoding": "json",
        "mapping": {
          "customers": "participants"
        },
        "host": [
          "http://demo-api.demo.svc.cluster.local:8080"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
]
